@startuml
title MODRISS Model-Driven Increment — Detailed Phase 1 View

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false

start
:Frame one valuable capability or event journey;
:Record requirements, quality scenarios, risks,\ndependencies and acceptance evidence;

repeat
  :Discover or revise the CIM slice;
  :Run structural conformance and the explicit\nuser/model semantic-validation workflow;
repeat while (G2 CIM acceptance rejected?) is (yes)
-> no;

:Run versioned CIM→PIM ETL into a generated target;
:Three-way reconcile generated baseline, previous\nbaseline and refined working PIM;
repeat
  :Refine services, events, contracts, data, state,\nworkflow, security, resilience, SLOs and portability;
repeat while (G3 PIM acceptance rejected?) is (yes)
-> no;

:Run versioned PIM→AWS PSM ETL and reconcile;
repeat
  :Refine AWS resources, IAM, network, storage,\nmessaging, compute, API, workflow and observability;
repeat while (G4 PSM acceptance rejected?) is (yes)
-> no;

:Generate reproducible EGL/EGX artifact baseline;
:Complete supported handwritten extensions;
:Run unit, contract, component, integration, NFR,\nsecurity, recovery and operational tests selected by risk;

if (G5 increment accepted?) then (yes)
  :Record exact model, transform, generator, artifact,\ntest and evidence revisions;
  stop
else (rework / defer)
  :Route every finding to its earliest authoritative\nmodel, generator, code or process source;
  detach
endif

legend bottom
  Assistant-generated model actions are gated only by structural Ecore/EMF
  conformance. Semantic EVL validation is an explicit user/model workflow.
endlegend
@enduml
